# Desktop-app topology: EVERYTHING is served by the aura-brain (8000 is squatted
# by Pollen's "Reachy Mini Control" app, hence 8020). Baked into every
# `npm run build` so a plain build always produces a working desktop console.
#
# U234: two things changed here, and both are load-bearing.
#
# 1. 127.0.0.1, not localhost. On Windows "localhost" resolves to ::1 first, so
#    the name can reach a different process holding the same port on the other
#    address family. That is how the app once loaded somebody else's dev server.
#
# 2. This is now a FALLBACK, not the answer. The desktop shell injects the port
#    it actually got into index.html (window.__AURA_RUNTIME__), so a busy 8020
#    no longer means a broken app. See src/lib/endpoints.ts.
#
# Dev against another host: override via a local .env.production.local.
VITE_BRAIN_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8020
VITE_ROBOT_RUNTIME_WS=ws://127.0.0.1:8020/ws/events
